# map to=hagiang label="HÀ GIANG"
This is *Vietnam*.
And way up at the very top… *Hà Giang*.

# title text="THE HÀ GIANG|LOOP" sub="explained honestly"

# intro place=oldquarter hero=dave mood=bored host=linh ask="Ever heard of\nthe Hà Giang Loop?" shout="SIGN. ME. UP."
Meet *Dave*. Dave is in Hà Nội. Dave is bored.
Linh knows a 4-day motorbike loop that fixes that.

# route stops="hagiang,quanba,yenminh,lungcu,dongvan,mapileng,meovac,dugia" loop=yes stats="≈ 300–350 km;of mountain road|3–4 DAYS;4 is the comfortable pace|∞ HAIRPINS;give or take"
The loop: roughly *300–350 km* of mountain road.
Most people ride it in *3–4 days*. Don't rush it in two.

# compare leftTitle="Ride it yourself" left=dave leftRide=yes leftMood=nervous leftPrice="250k–400k ₫;$10–16;bike, per day" rightTitle="Easy Rider" right=easyrider rightRide=yes rightMood=cool rightPrice="2–3.2M ₫;$80–125;driver + bike, per day" checked="Oct 2026"
Rent a bike yourself, or hire an *Easy Rider* who drives while you look.
Riding yourself needs a *1968 IDP* with a motorbike endorsement.

# ride place=hagiang hero=dave stop=yes sign="CỔNG TRỜI" sub="QUẢN BẠ · HEAVEN'S GATE" react=starstruck
Day 1: north through Quản Bạ to *Heaven’s Gate*.
The name is… not an exaggeration.

# gag place=hagiang hero=dave mood=happy react=scared punch="800 M DOWN?!"
Day 2: *Mã Pì Lèng Pass*.
Pull over to look. Never look while riding.

# social place=homestay hero=dave host=hmong_grandpa cheer="MỘT, HAI, BA… DZÔ!" toasts=3
Nights: homestays, home cooking, and *“happy water”* — corn wine.
Vietnam has a *zero* alcohol limit. No riding until it’s gone.

# list title="When to go" host=linh items="Sep — green rice terraces|Oct–Nov — buckwheat flowers (busiest)|Mar–Apr — plum & pear blossoms|!Jun–Aug — landslide season"
Best windows: *September–November* and *March–April*.
June to August is landslide season. Skip it.

# payoff place=hagiang hero=dave host=linh title="HÀ GIANG|LOOP" sub="4 days · ≈300–350 km · 0 regrets"
Dave is no longer bored.
